  ]}
>
  <p>
    HelloNotes is a <strong>local-first</strong> application. Your notes are stored as plain files
    on your own device, in a folder you select.
    <strong>We do not collect, transmit, sell, or have access to your notes or any personal data.</strong>
  </p>

  <div class="my-6 rounded-card border border-line bg-card px-[26px] py-[22px]">
    <strong>In short:</strong> no account, no analytics, no tracking, no servers. Your data never
    leaves your Mac unless you explicitly choose to sync it somewhere yourself.
  </div>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing. HelloNotes has no analytics, no telemetry, no advertising identifiers, and no user
    accounts. We do not operate any server that receives your data.
  </p>

  <h2>Your notes</h2>
  <p>
    Your notes are ordinary Markdown files in a folder on your device that you choose with the
    “Select Vault Folder” command. They remain under your control and can be read or edited by any
    other application.
  </p>

  <h2>On-device intelligence</h2>
  <p>
    The optional Summarise, Suggest Tags/Links, Expand and “Ask your vault” features use Apple’s
    on-device Foundation Models framework. Your note content is processed locally on your Mac and is
    <strong>not</strong> sent to us or to any third party. These features only appear on hardware with
    Apple Intelligence available.
  </p>

  <h2>Version control (Git)</h2>
  <p>
    If you choose to use the built-in Git features and configure your own remote repository, your
    notes are sent only to the destination <em>you</em> configure, under your control. HelloNotes is
    not that destination and does not receive a copy.
  </p>

  <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
  <p>HelloNotes does not collect data from anyone, including children, and is rated 4+.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    Because we hold no user data, there is nothing for us to disclose, share, or delete on request.
    If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted on this page.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:info@hellotham.com">info@hellotham.com</a>.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
